## I want an excuse to use it

My enthusiasm for variable fonts as an expressive runtime is sitting at about <span class="chart" aria-hidden="true">{p:85}</span><span class="kh-u-sr-only">(roughly 85 percent)</span>, while my likelihood of actually reaching for Datatype on the next chart I ship is somewhere around <span class="chart" aria-hidden="true">{p:25}</span><span class="kh-u-sr-only">(roughly 25 percent)</span>. The gap between those two pies is basically the whole post.

Frank's [specimen site](https://franktisellano.github.io/datatype/) is worth a visit on its own; the variable-axis sliders and live examples are a small showcase of typographic care.

